1. e4 { Do you remember the first moves? } 1... e5 2. Nf3 { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gb8c6] } 2... Nc6 3. Bc4 { Remember? 🤨🧐🤔 } { [%csl Gf5][%cal Gf7f5] } 3... f5 4. exf5 { [%csl Ge4][%cal Ge5e4] } 4... e4 5. Qe2 { Black tries to be smart and pins our pawn. 🫤 But instead of smart, this is a mistake! } { [%csl Re8,Ge7][%cal Re2e8,Gd8e7] } 5... Qe7 { Nice. } 6. Ng1 { [%csl Gf6,Rh5][%cal Gg8f6,Re2h5] } 6... Nf6 { Developing and stopping Qh5+. } 7. d3 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gc6d4] } 7... Nd4 { Pouncing on the black queen. } { [%csl Re2][%cal Rd4e2] } 8. Qd1 { How can you take advantage of white's king? } { [%csl Re1][%cal Re7e1] } 8... Nxc2+!! (8... exd3+ { This is strong, but not as much as our main option. }) 9. Qxc2 { [%csl Gd3][%cal Ge4d3] } 9... exd3+ { -5.5. White's queen is gone. Great job! 😀 } { [%csl Rc2,Re1,Re2][%cal Rd3c2,Re7e1,Rd3e2] } *


